earch\n\n#### NLP\n\n#### Teaching AI to translate 100s of spoken and written languages in real time\n\nTo enable translations for low-resource languages & to prep for future real-time speech to speech translations, we’re expanding our automatic data set creation techniques, working to overcome modeling challenges, and finding new ways to evaluate MT results.\n\nFebruary 23, 2022\n\nLearn More\n\nBlog\n\nFebruary 14, 2022\n\n#### Research\n\n#### A new resource to help measure fairness in AI speech recognition systems\n\nFairness is an important concern for speech recognition systems, just as for other AI applications. So we’ve created and released a unique new resource for measuring how well these systems work for different groups of people\n\nFebruary 14, 2022\n\nLearn More\n\nBlog\n\nJanuary 24, 2022\n\n#### Research\n\n#### Introducing the AI Research SuperCluster — Meta’s cutting-edge AI supercomputer for AI research\n\nIntroducing the AI Research SuperCluster — Meta’s cutting-edge AI supercomputer for AI research\n\nJanuary 24, 2022\n\nLearn More\n\nBlog\n\nFebruary 08, 2022\n\n#### ML Applications\n\n#### Computer Vision\n\n#### Creating better virtual backdrops for video calling, remote presence, and AR\n\nTo improve background blurring, virtual backgrounds, and many other AR effects, Meta has built and deployed new high-performance segmentation models. These systems, along with other significantly improved segmentation models, are in production to improve people’s experiences using Portal, Messenger, Reels, Instagram, and Messenger.\n\nFebruary 08, 2022\n\nLearn More\n\nBlog\n\nJanuary 20, 2022\n\n#### Research\n\n#### Data2vec: The first high-performance self-supervised algorithm that works for speech, vision, and text\n\nWe’ve built data2vec, the first general high-performance self-supervised algorithm for speech, vision, and text. When applied to different modalities, it matches or outperforms the best self-supervised algorithms.\n\nJanuary 20, 2022\n\nL