rful, flexible, and accessible era for computer vision\n\nThe future of AI is in creating systems that can learn directly from whatever information they’re given — whether it’s text, images, or another type of data — without relying on carefully curated and labeled data sets to teach them how to recognize objects in a photo, interpret a block of text, or perform any of the countless other tasks that we ask it to.\n\nMarch 04, 2021\n\nLearn More\n\nBlog\n\nMarch 04, 2021\n\n#### Research\n\n#### Self-supervised learning: The dark matter of intelligence\n\nHow can we build machines with human-level intelligence? There’s a limit to how far the field of AI can go with supervised learning alone. Here's why self-supervised learning is one of the most promising ways to make significant progress in AI.\n\nMarch 04, 2021\n\nLearn More\n\nBlog\n\nMarch 03, 2021\n\n#### Research\n\n#### Facebook AI’s RAISE program: A new pathway to make careers in AI more accessible\n\nCareers in AI should be open to everyone with the curiosity to make an impact in this rapidly evolving field. With that in mind and to build a new path into the field, we’re launching RAISE (Rotational AI Science & Engineering), a 24-month program for experienced engineers from a wide variety of disciplines. Learn more:\n\nMarch 03, 2021\n\nLearn More\n\nBlog\n\nJanuary 20, 2021\n\n#### NLP\n\n#### ML Applications\n\n#### How AI learns to help finish your sentences\n\nPredictive text makes communicating with colleagues, family, and friends easier and more convenient. Here's how AI makes it work.\n\nJanuary 20, 2021\n\nLearn More\n\nBlog\n\nJanuary 22, 2021\n\n#### Research\n\n#### NLP\n\n#### A new open data set for multilingual speech research\n\nFacebook AI is releasing Multilingual LibriSpeech (MLS), a large-scale, open source data set designed to help advance research in automatic speech recognition (ASR) across multiple languages.\n\nJanuary 22, 2021\n\nLearn More\n\nBlog\n\nSeptember 28, 2020\n\n#### ML Ap